<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Walls and doors (system 16: Building). Ungated by research — a wood/stone wall is not a technology any
    more than a club is (see research.unlocks-content's own note on the club). Costed in wood, the material
    every settlement starts able to gather.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Wall</defName>
    <label>wall</label>
    <description>A solid wall, providing structure and insulation.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Building</thingClass>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <pathCost>10000</pathCost>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>300</MaxHitPoints>
      <Insulation>100</Insulation>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>5</WoodLog>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Door</defName>
    <label>door</label>
    <description>A doorway through a wall.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Door</thingClass>
    <!--
      Deviation (see SimWorld.Building.Door's own remarks): real RimWorld doors swing open for an
      approaching pawn and are otherwise impassable; this pass's Door is always Standable (open) — no swing
      state, no faction-allowed check. fillPercent stays 1 so RoomTracker still treats it as a room boundary
      (a doorway still separates two Rooms; RoomGroup re-merges them thermally) even though it never blocks
      movement.
    -->
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <Insulation>1</Insulation>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>4</WoodLog>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <!--
    Bed and StorageHut (building.initiative — SettlementConstructionInitiative's own buildable Defs): what a
    settlement decides for itself it needs, not player-designed content. Ungated by research and wood-costed
    like Wall/Door above, for the same reason. WorkToBuild/MaxHitPoints/costList are SimWorld's own figures —
    RimWorld's real bed/storage-structure costs were not sourceable from this sandbox — chosen to sit between
    Door and Heater in effort; pinned by ConstructionInitiativeTests' end-to-end build rather than trusted as
    a literal (CLAUDE.md's own rule for untraceable numbers).

    Bed is wired into Need_Rest/JobGiver_GetRest (AI/RestUtility.cs, AI/JobDriver_LayDown.cs): a pawn seeking
    rest claims the nearest reachable, unclaimed Bed and sleeps faster there than on the ground
    (Need_Rest.BedRestEffectiveness) rather than always sleeping in place. This system still only decides
    whether the settlement *has* enough beds — placing one per citizen — not who sleeps in which; there is no
    ownership/assignment concept here, matching what RimWorld actually needs for an unowned, first-come bed.

    Its statBases' own <BedRestEffectiveness> (task #104) is a different stat under the same RimWorld name —
    Need_Rest's constant above governs the rest *need*'s gain rate and was never wired to content; this one is
    read by Stats.StatPart_BedStat off the live bed and feeds ImmunityGainSpeed/TendUtility instead. See
    Health.HealthStatDefOf's own doc comment for why the two coexist rather than being unified.

    Bed is 1x2, RimWorld's own <size>(1,2)</size> for a single bed (a double bed is 2x2 there; none ships
    here). Blueprint_Bed and Frame_Bed declare no size: they derive it from entityToBuild (Thing.Size), so
    they cannot disagree with this. Position is the head end, the bed's one sleeping slot
    (AI.BedUtility.GetSleepingSlotPos), and the footprint runs from there the way the bed faces
    (Map.GenAdj.OccupiedRect).
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Bed</defName>
    <label>bed</label>
    <description>A simple sleeping pallet. Every settler wants one of their own.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Building</thingClass>
    <size>(1,2)</size>
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0</fillPercent>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>180</WorkToBuild>
      <!-- Task #104 (system: Health — medicine): x1.07, RimWorld's own "regular bed" value
           (rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Immunity_gain_speed and rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Bed both give it), read by
           Stats.StatPart_BedStat off whichever bed a pawn is actually lying in. MedicalTendQualityOffset is
           left unset — RimWorld's regular bed carries none either; only a hospital bed (not shipped here)
           is ever above zero. -->
      <BedRestEffectiveness>1.07</BedRestEffectiveness>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>8</WoodLog>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>StorageHut</defName>
    <label>storage hut</label>
    <description>A roofed hut for keeping goods out of the weather.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Building</thingClass>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0</fillPercent>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>320</WorkToBuild>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>25</WoodLog>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
